# Regression testing

New features and refactors must **not break existing behavior**. Treat regression protection as part of the feature, not optional cleanup.

## Mindset

- **Preserve contracts**: matching rules (AND/OR), start-date parsing from titles only, localStorage keys (`sth-settings-v2`, `sth-history-v2`), and user-visible panel behavior must still work after your change—unless the task explicitly documents a breaking change.
- **Test the blast radius, not just the diff**: Ask what existing code paths your change touches (row scraping, date parsing, match, sort, panel sync).

## Test inventory (this repo)

| Area | Automated checks | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Pure lib** (`src/lib/`) | `npm run test` | Dates, match, settings merge, sort, stats, detect, row fixtures |
| **Extension package** | `npm run build` | `dist/sth-extension/` must contain `manifest.json` + `content.js` |
| **Lint / types** | `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` | Required on PRs |

```bash
npm run check
```

## Verification matrix (by change type)

| You changed… | Required checks |
| --- | --- |
| **Date parsing, match, sort, settings** | Add/extend unit tests; `npm run test` |
| **DOM scraping (`rows.ts`, start column)** | jsdom fixture test; load unpacked extension on a tickets and a journeys list |
| **Panel UI** | `npm run build`; manual smoke of filters, collapse, statistics |
| **Manifest / build** | `npm run build`; confirm zip still loads unpacked |
| **Cross-cutting refactor** | `npm run check` plus tickets + journeys smoke |

## Manual smoke paths

1. **Tickets** — Idle highlight, status tags, AND/OR, saved views, sort, open marked tabs.
2. **Journeys** — Start date column, start-date tags, extras (progress / start within), statistics without storing names.
3. **Reload** — Rebuild, reload the extension card, refresh Freshservice; a single panel instance remains.

Report which commands and smokes you ran when claiming completion.
